## 414. Third Maximum Number

### Approach

--  Maintain 3 variables: `max`, `secMax`, and `thirdMax`.
--  Traverse the array once and skip duplicate values.
--  If the current number is greater than `max`, shift `max → secMax → thirdMax`.
--  Else if it is greater than `secMax`, shift `secMax → thirdMax`.
--  Else if it is greater than `thirdMax`, update `thirdMax`.
--  If 3 distinct maximum values don't exist, return `max`.
--  Use `long` variables so `Integer.MIN_VALUE` can safely be a placeholder.

Time : `O(n)`
Space : `O(1)`

SOLUTION : 
class Solution {
    public int thirdMax(int[] nums) {
        long max = Long.MIN_VALUE;
        long secMax = Long.MIN_VALUE;
        long thirdMax = Long.MIN_VALUE;
        for (int num : nums) {
            if (num == max || num == secMax || num == thirdMax) {
                continue;
            }
            if (num > max) {
                thirdMax = secMax;
                secMax = max;
                max = num;
            } else if (num > secMax) {
                thirdMax = secMax;
                secMax = num;
            } else if(num > thirdMax){
                thirdMax = num;
            }

        }
        if(thirdMax == Long.MIN_VALUE) {
            return (int)max;
        }
        return (int)thirdMax;
    }
}
